{
  "raw": {
    "https://clsbe.lisboa.ucp.pt/system/files/assets/files/faculty-position-marketing-2026_1.pdf": {
      "title": "FACULTY POSITION IN QUANTITATIVE MARKETING",
      "description": " \nPalma de Cima, 1649-023 Lisboa \nTel. +351 217 270 250 \nwww.clsbe.lisboa.ucp.pt   \n \n \n \n \nFACULTY POSITION IN QUANTITATIVE MARKETING \nCatólica Lisbon School of Business and Economics, Portugal \n \n \n \nCatólica Lisbon School of Business and Economics (Católica-Lisbon SBE) invites applications for a full-time tenure-\ntrack Assistant Professor position in Quantitative Marketing, beginning in September 2027.  \nWe seek an outstanding scholar whose research and teaching will contribute to the next stage of the Marketing \ngroup's development and reinforce the School's position as one of Europe's leading research -oriented business \nschools. Applicants should have completed, or expect to complete, a PhD before the appointment date. \n \nA Strategic Opportunity \nThe Marketing group at Católica-Lisbon SBE  has established internationally recognized strengths in consumer \nbehavior, branding, marketing communications, digital marketing, and consumer decision making. As marketing is \nbeing reshaped by advances in data, artificial intelligence, and digital techno logies, the School is making a strategic \ninvestment to expand its expertise in quantitative and technology-enabled marketing. \nThe ideal candidate will play an important role in shaping this next phase of development. Beyond contributing to \nteaching, the new faculty member is expected to build an internationally visible research program and foster \ninterdisciplinary collaboration across the School, particularly with colleagues in Operations & Data Science. \n \nResearch Profile \nWe welcome applications from candidates with proven research interests in one or more of the following areas: \n• Marketing Analytics and Customer Insights \n• Artificial Intelligence in Marketing \n• Marketing Technology (MarTech) \n• Customer Experience Analytics \n• Pricing and Revenue Management \n• Digital Platforms and Data-Driven Marketing \nWe are interested in scholars addressing important marketing questions using rigorous empirical, econometric, \ncomputational, or machine -learning approaches. Outstanding candidates working in closely related areas of \nquantitative marketing are strongly encouraged to apply. \n \nWhat We Offer \nCatólica-Lisbon SBE is a research-intensive institution that provides an environment designed to support ambitious \nscholarship. Faculty are expected to pursue research aimed at the leading journals in marketing and related \ndisciplines. The School offers competitive compensation, substantial research support, funding for conferences and \ndata acquisition, an active international seminar program, and teaching loads that allow substantial time for research. \nFaculty also benefit from extensive opportunities for collaboration across disciplines, a highly international academic \ncommunity, and a collegial culture that values intellectual curiosity, research excellence, and innovation in teaching. \n \n \n \n \n \nPalma de Cima, 1649-023 Lisboa \nTel. +351 217 270 250 \nwww.clsbe.lisboa.ucp.pt   \n \n \nCandidate Qualifications \nApplicants for the Assistant Professor position should demonstrate outstanding potential for publishing in top -tier \njournals. Candidates at more senior levels should have an established record of high -quality publications in top \njournals in marketing or a closely related field, excellence in teaching, and the ability to strengthen the research profile \nof the Marketing group. \nWe seek scholars who combine substantive marketing insight with methodological rigor. Proven experience with \nanalytical and computational tools (e.g., R, Python, SQL, Julia, Stata, or similar) is important.  \nWe particularly value candidates who actively contribute to a vibrant academic community through collaboration, \nintellectual engagement, and collegiality, and who are enthusiastic about participating in the day -to-day life of the \ndepartment, including regular on-campus interaction with colleagues, doctoral students, and students. \n \nThe Marketing Group \nThe Marketing group consists of internationally trained faculty with publications in leading journals including the \nJournal of Marketing, Journal of Marketing Research, Journal of Consumer Research, Journal of Consumer \nPsychology, Marketing Science, and other premier outlets. The group combines a collaborative culture with ambitious \nresearch goals and is committed to developing internationally recognized scholarship while delivering outstanding \nteaching across undergraduate, master's, MBA, and executive education programs. \nThis appointment reflects the group's long -term vision of broadening its expertise in quantitative and technology -\nenabled marketing while building on its established strengths in behavioral research. \n \nAbout Católica-Lisbon SBE \nCATÓLICA-LISBON is consistently ranked among Europe's leading business schools and holds the prestigious triple \naccreditation (AACSB, EQUIS and AMBA). The School's programs are taught entirely in English and attract students \nand faculty from around the wor ld. Faculty are affiliated with CUBE, one of Portugal's leading research centers in \neconomics and management, providing an excellent platform for interdisciplinary research and international \ncollaboration. \nLocated in Lisbon, one of Europe's most vibrant ca pitals, Católica-Lisbon SBE offers an exceptional quality of life \ntogether with a dynamic international academic environment. \n \nApplication Procedure \nApplications should include: \n• Cover letter \n• Curriculum vitae \n• Research statement \n• Teaching statement \n• Job market paper or representative publications \n• Three letters of recommendation (for junior candidates) \nPriority consideration will be given to applications received by October 1st. Applications will remain open until the \nposition is filled. Initial interviews will be conducted online, followed by campus visits for shortlisted candidates.  \nFor further information, please contact the Faculty Recruitment Office and the Chair of the Search Committee. \n \n \nApplications should be submitted to the Faculty Recruitment Office (internationalrecruit.clsbe@ucp.pt).  \nAny questions regarding the position may be directed to Prof. Daniel Fernandes (daniel.fernandes@ucp.pt). \n "
    },
    "https://clsbe.lisboa.ucp.pt/system/files/assets/files/1.-opening-notice-cube-2bii-debiasify-5-2025-correccao-v2-1.pdf": {
      "title": "Opening Notice",
      "description": "Opening Notice \nResearch Initiation Fellowship (BII)  \nReference: CUBE_2BII_DEBIASIFY_5_2025 \nCUBE -  Católica  Lisbon  Research  Unit  in  Business  and  Economics  at  Católica  Lisbon  School  of \nBusiness & Economics, Universidade Católica Portuguesa, is awarding a 2 (two) Research Initiation \nFellowship (BII) in the scientific field of Psychology for the development of research in the frame \nof the reference project - 2024.07497.IACDC/2024 , supported by the measure “RE-C05-i08. M04 - \nSupport a program of R&D projects for development and implementation of advanced \ncybersecurity, artificial intelligence and data science systems in public administration, to  \nreinforce the process of digital transformation and digitization of science and support services of \nthe National Science and Technology System (NSTS) , of the Recovery and Resilience Plan – PRR, \nwithin the scope of the financing contract signed between the Recover Portugal Mission Structure \n(EMRP) and the Foundation for Science and Technology I.P. (FCT), as an intermediate \nbeneficiary. \nABOUT THE PROJECT \nThis research project aims to improve hiring decisions and combat workplace \ndiscrimination through artificial intelligence (AI)-based advisory systems. The focus is on \npromoting fairer decisions by reducing the influence of stereotypes and human biases. \nAlthough AI has the potential to enhance decision quality, there is often an aversion to its use. \nThe project explores ways to increase trust in AI systems, such as introducing certification labels, \nwithout fostering blind trust. \nTo this end, several experimental studies will be conducted, and their results will form the basis \nfor developing an AI application. \nADMISSION REQUIREMENTS \nAt the time of application, candidates must be enrolled or accepted to be enrolled in \nan undergraduate program in the scientific area of Psychology. \nCandidates with a bachelor's degree are also encouraged to participate. \nOther requirements are the following: \n• Good data collection and analysis skills.\n• Strong quantitative skills.\n• Excellent command of the English language.\n• Ability to work in an organized and autonomous m anner.\nPreferential requirements: \n• Preference will be given to candidates who can work with statistical software such as SPSS, R, or\nJASP.\n \n \n  \n• Interest and experience in Psychology research will be valued. \n• Programming skills for experimental studies in software such as Qualtrics or e -prime will also be \nvalued. \n• Preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate programming ability. \n• Experience in academic writing will be valued. \n \nWORK PLAN AND GOALS \nThe research fellow will conduct academic research in the field of Psychology. The main duties of \nthe researcher are: \n• Literature review. \n• Study schedule. \n• Data collection and analysis. \n• Writing outputs. \n \nAPPLICABLE REGULATIONS \nResearch Fellow Statute, approved by Law No. 40/2004, of August 18, in the current wording \nconferred by Decree -Law No. 123/2019, of August 28; current Regulation of Fellowships of \nFundação para a Ciência e Tecnologia, I.P. (Regulation No. 950/2019 of December 16th); Regulation \nof Fellowships of Universidade Católica Portuguesa. \n \nWORKPLACE AND SCIENTIFIC GUIDANCE \nThe workplace is the Católica Lisbon School of Business & Economics, Universidade  Católica \nPortuguesa, in Lisbon, and the work will be developed under the scientific guidance of Professor \nFilipa de Almeida. \n \nFELLOWSHIP’S DURATION AND START DATE \nThe fellowship will be awarded for 7 months, with exclusive commitment. The fellowship may be \nrenewed up to the fullest extent permitted by applicable regulations. The renewal of the fellowship \ncontract depends on the research fellow’s evaluation concerning the accomplishment of the work \nplan, the fulfil lment of personal requirements for the fellowship renewal , and the availability of \nfunding for the project. \nThe fellowship is expected to start in June 2025. \n \nMONTHLY MAINTENANCE ALLOWANCE \nThe fellowship’s maintenance allowance is 651,12€ per month, according to the table of values of \nthe grants awarded directly by FCT, I.P. in the Country.  Further information at \nhttps://www.fct.pt/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Tabela_valores_SMM_2025.pdf.  \n \n \n  \n The fellowship will be paid monthly by bank transfer. \nThe fellowship holder will be covered by personal accident insurance.  \nIf not covered by any social protection scheme, the fellowship holder can ensure the right to Social \nSecurity through adherence to the Voluntary Social Security scheme, under \"Código dos Regimes \nContributivos do Sistema Previdencial de Segurança Social\". Provided that the awarded fellowship \nhas a minimum duration of 6 months, the fellowship holder will be entitled to assume, by UCP, the \ncharges resulting from the contributions  that apply to the first bracket referred to in article 36 of \nDecree-Law no. 40/89 , of 1 February, with the increase in charges arising from the option for a \nhigher incidence base on its own. \n \nSELECTION METHOD \nThe candidates’ final classification shall be presented on a scale of 0 to 20. \n \nThe evaluation will be carried out in 2 phases: \n1. Firstly, candidates are evaluated based on 3 criteria, based on the scientific and academic \ncurriculum (PC): \nA. Academic curriculum: 50%. \nB. Demonstrated knowledge of the work area, including previous research experience: 30%. \nC. Data collection and analysis skills: 20% \nPC = (0.50 x A) + (0.30 x B) + (0.20 x C) \n2. A minimum of 15 points is required for a candidate to be considered eligible for the position and \nto proceed to the second phase, which involves an interview (E). The interview can be in person or \ndone online. The final classification will be obtained as follows: \nCF = (PC x 0.6) + (E x 0.4) \nThe selection panel reserves the right not to select any candidate if it considers that none of the \ncandidates has the required profile. \n \nCOMPOSITION OF THE SELECTION PANEL \nPresident of the Jury: Professor Filipa de Almeida (fellow supervisor) \nEffective Member: Professor Cristina Mendonça (fellow supervisor; Instituto Superior Técnico - \nUniversidade de Lisboa) \nEffective Member: Professor Ian Scott (fellow supervisor; Nova IMS - Universidade Nova de Lisboa) \nSubstitute member(s): Professor João Santos (research fellow; ISPA) \n \nREQUIRED DOCUMENTS FOR APPLICATION \nApplications are to be submitted in English and PDF format. \n \n \n  \nApplications shall include the following documents: \n1. A letter elaborating on the motivations and objectives for applying to the BII fellowship. \n2. Curriculum Vitae including all the elements to access the admission requirements, namely all the \nresearch fellowships previously awarded, if applicable; \n3. Proof of enrol lment in the required Bachelor's degree program or proof of meeting the \nrequirements for enrollment in the required program. \n \nDEADLINES AND SUBMISSION OF APPLICATIONS \nRequired documents should be sent by e-mail to catolica-lisbon-research@ucp.pt from 07th May to \n20th  May 2025 (until 5 pm Lisbon time) with the reference Subject: CUBE_2BII_DEBIASIFY_5_2025 \n- #Candidate's name#. \nNo document that should have been submitted at the application stage may be presented after the \ndeadline set for this purpose in the opening notice. Failure to comply with the deadline set for the \nsubmission of the application, as well as the lack of submission or late submission of the documents \nreferred to in this point, will result in exclusion from the competition. False statements provided by \nthe candidates are punishable by law. \n \nDELIBERATION AND RELEASE OF THE RESULTS \nThe selection panel deliberates by adopting and disclosing selection criteria. Minutes of panel \nmeetings shall include a summary of the meeting content. After application of the selection criteria, \nthe panel shall prepare a ranked list of approved candidates and their respective classifications. \nThe ranked list of candidates will be published within 90 working days after the deadline of the \napplications on the CATÓLICA-LISBON website https://www.clsbe.lisboa.ucp.pt/research/research-\npositions. Candidates will be notified by e-mail once this list is made available. \nIn the 10 working days after the communication of the final decision, the selected candidate must \nconfirm in writing his/her availability to initiate the fellowship in the proposed date. In case of \nunavailability, the offer will be made to the next candidate in the ranked list. \n \nPRIOR HEARING, COMPLAINTS, AND APPEALS \nIn case of unfavorable decision, candidates will have 10 working days after notification to appeal in \na prior hearing, should they wish it, under the terms of the Code of Administrative Procedures. The \nfinal decision may be subject to a complaint within 15 working days or an appeal within 30 working \ndays, with both durations beginning on the date of the initial notification. The complaint or appeal \nshould be addressed to the Rector’s Office (Reitoria) of Universidade Católica Portuguesa. After this \nnotification, and in case there are no allegations, the results will become definitive. Ineligible \ncandidates will be notified by email, with details of the missing eligibility elements. \n \nPRIVACY POLICY \n \n \n  \nUniversidade Católica Portuguesa is the controller responsible for the processing of Personal Data \nin accordance with Regulation (EU) 2016/679 – General Regulation on Data Protection. \nThe personal data submitted within the scope of this tender procedure is processed within the \nframework of said tender procedure only, and will be treated by Universidade Católica Portuguesa \nwith the purpose of verifying the fulfillment, by the candidates,  of the assumptions established in \nthe applicable legislation for their contracting. Opposition to the processing of data by the \ncandidates will make it impossible to accept the application and, therefore, to analyze and evaluate \nit.  \nThe personal data of the Data Subject, if it be indispensable for the fulfillment of the obligations of \nUniversidade Católica Portuguesa, may be conveyed to third parties, namely to the Financing \nEntities identified in this announcement. \nThe data retention period shall correspond to the legally defined period of five years. \nThe Data Subject is entitled to oppose to the collection and processing of data, has the right to \nverification, the right to rectification, the right to deletion, and the right to restriction of processing \nof the data collected. However, the exercise of such rights may be excluded when the personal data \nis used to protect public interest, namely in the detection and prevention of crimes or when subject \nto professional rules of confidentiality. \nThe Data Subject has the right of access and portability of the data. \nRights of Personal Data Subjects: https://www.ucp.pt/rights-data-subjects. \nFor purposes of exercising the respective rights, contact the University through the e-mail address \ncompliance.rgpd@ucp.pt or by using the address found at the end of this announcement, through \nthe means set out in \"Contacts for clarification\".  \nThe Data Subject is always entitled to contact and file a complaint with the Comissão Nacional de \nProteção de Dados (Portuguese Supervisory Authority for Personal Data). \n \nNON-DISCRIMINATION AND EQUAL ACCESS POLICY  \nUniversidade Católica Portuguesa actively promotes a non-discrimination and equal access policy, \nwherefore no candidate can be privileged, benefited, impaired or deprived of any rights \nwhatsoever, or be exempt of any duties based on their ancestry, age, ge nder, sexual orientation, \nmarital status, family status, family and economic conditions, instruction, social origin or condition, \ngenetic heritage, reduced working capacity, disability, chronic illness, nationality, ethnic origin or \nrace, territory of orig in, language, religion, political or ideological convictions, and union \nmembership. \n \nCONTACTS FOR CLARIFICATION \nUniversidade Católica Portuguesa \nCATÓLICA-LISBON \nCUBE  \nPalma de Cima, 1649-023 Lisboa \nTel. 217214122 \n \n \n  \nE-mail: catolica-lisbon-research@ucp.pt \n \nHuman Resources Department \nE-mail: drh.sede@ucp.pt  \n "
    }
